Context — reference material only; do not repeat any of it in your response.

Requirement 03.14.02 — Malicious Code Protection
Provide protection from malicious code at designated locations within organizational systems.
03.14.02.b: Protection from malicious code at designated locations is provided

Assessment objectives (a coverage checklist — do NOT copy their wording):
- protection from malicious code at designated locations is provided

Evidence excerpts:
--- [Endpoint_and_Perimeter_Malware_Protection_Standard_v2.3.docx] (excerpt)
4.1 Designated Protection Points. Tamarind Aerospace applies malicious code scanning at three enforcement locations: (a) all Windows and macOS endpoints, (b) the network perimeter, and (c) email and file collaboration services. Endpoints run Sophos Intercept X Advanced with XDR, with deep learning, exploit prevention, and CryptoGuard enabled. Tamper protection is required on all devices. Intune compliance policy 'TA-Win-Baseline' marks a device noncompliant if the Sophos service has not checked in for 24 hours. At the perimeter, both PA-440 firewalls apply the 'TA-Strict-AV' Antivirus and WildFire Analysis profiles to every allow rule between the Trust, Shop-Floor and Untrust zones. Microsoft Defender for Office 365 Safe Attachments (Dynamic Delivery) and Safe Links protect Exchange Online, SharePoint and Teams in the GCC tenant. The IT Manager reviews coverage every quarter.
--- [PA440_Security_Profile_Export_2024-05-14.txt] (excerpt)
profile-group TA-Default {
  virus TA-Strict-AV;
  spyware TA-Strict-AS;
  vulnerability TA-Strict-VP;
  wildfire-analysis TA-WF-All;
}
virus TA-Strict-AV {
  decoder http  action reset-both; wildfire-action reset-both;
  decoder smtp  action reset-both; wildfire-action reset-both;
  decoder ftp   action reset-both; wildfire-action reset-both;
  decoder smb   action reset-both; wildfire-action reset-both;
