4.3 Automated Processes and Service Accounts
Any script, agent, integration, or scheduled task that logs into Quillfeather Software systems must use its own dedicated identity. It may not reuse a person's credentials. Every service identity must have:
(a) a name starting with "svc-" or the vendor agent name, recorded in the Service Account Inventory;
(b) a named human owner who answers for what the process does;
(c) a documented purpose and a minimum scope of access;
(d) a Jira Service Management request (ACCESS project) approved by the IT Administrator before it is created.
Interactive login is disabled for service identities in JumpCloud (Bound groups: "Service-NoLogin"). OAuth apps connected to Google Workspace are limited to the allowlist under Admin Console > Security > API Controls. Unlisted apps are blocked. Owners recertify the inventory every quarter. An identity with no owner is disabled within 5 business days.

4.2 Baseline Requirements for CUI-Handling Providers
Any external service that stores, processes, or transmits controlled technical data (customer drawings, CAM programs, ITAR/CUI-marked specs) must meet the following before the contract is signed:
(a) FedRAMP Moderate authorization or equivalent, or a documented SPRS score of at least 88 with a POA&M;
(b) FIPS 140-2/140-3 validated encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+) and at rest;
(c) Notification of any incident affecting Pellucid data within 72 hours, with forensic images kept for 90 days;
(d) Data hosted only in U.S. regions, with U.S.-person support staff;
(e) MFA for all provider admin access.
The IT Manager writes these terms into the contract language. Procurement must not issue a PO until the Security Addendum (Form SEC-07) has been signed.

